{"stamp": "1791723939367000468-1345657", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Equivalence.lean", "line_start": 14, "line_end": 22, "replacement": "In `Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Localization/Predicate.lean`, the lemma\n`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_target` already showed that the predicate of localized\ncategories is unchanged when we replace the target category (i.e. the candidate localized\ncategory) by an equivalent category.\nIn this file, we show the same for the source category\n(`Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalence_source`).\nMore generally, `Functor.IsLocalization.of_equivalences` shows that we may replace both the\nsource and target categories by equivalent categories. This is obtained using\n`Localization.isEquivalence` which provide a sufficient condition in order to show\nthat a functor between localized categories is an equivalence."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
